# Weapon behavior evidence

- Read docs/WEAPON_BEHAVIOR.md before adding or changing a weapon.
- Verify character -> WeaponData enum -> attack prefab -> projectile -> renderer/material/audio references. Sword2 and HeroSword27 are distinct.
- Determine quantity behavior per weapon: sequential burst, simultaneous volley, angular spread or another mode. Never infer a fan from quantity alone or copy Sword rules to another weapon.
- Separate attack cooldown, burst spacing, individual projectile lifetime and hit history. A later attack may hit again; do not share one hit set across a temporal burst without evidence.
- Compose native local transforms/rotations with world facing and the documented handedness conversion. Test the rendered atlas frames; a vector test does not prove visual parity.
- Preserve native metadata; put user-requested size/speed overrides in web tuning, clearly labeled.
- Record unverified runtime formulas in docs/TEMPORARY_IMPLEMENTATIONS.md. Empty dump.cs bodies and filenames do not prove behavior.
- Keep provisional fallback behavior explicit and per weapon; never report full native parity from file extraction alone.

- Deliver weapon changes coherently: attack timing/quantity, VFX, audio and lifecycle. User preference (2026-11-13): the user will perform gameplay/visual/audio feel tests. Default to build/type checking and only necessary focused logic checks. Avoid repeated browser sessions, screenshots or broad test rounds unless a concrete issue requires them or the user asks. Provide a short manual test list when useful. Updated user preference (2026-11-13): commit and push completed authorized changes automatically after appropriate checks; notify the user before a phase transition. See skills/warcore-development/SKILL.md. A later explicit request to wait or keep work local takes precedence.
